.env
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# `dg report` writes here by default. It is a rendering of the graph in the project
# directory (the only path that exists on both sides of the container bind mount), so it
# lands where a stray `git add .` would pick it up.
decision-graph-report.html

# The demo videos are rendered output: ~200MB of it, from the scripts alongside this file.
# Same reason as the line above -- they land in the project directory, which is where a stray
# `git add .` looks -- but with a consequence that entry does not have. A 66MB capture that
# lands once stays in every future clone, because git does not forget a blob it has seen.
#
# The generators are committed; what they produce is not. Re-render with `generate_video.py`,
# `record_terminal_video.py`, or `record_dg_menu_video.py`.
*.mp4
*.aac
*.srt
demo_video_assets/
menu_recording_assets/
terminal_recording_assets/
subtitles_audio_assets/
video_analysis_frames/
video_fine_frames/
